raphael: Adreno 640 (SM8150) in the sweet_a630 GPU driver

The Poco F1 driver (patches 0103, 0180-0189, 0214, 0229, 0234-0237, 0251)
gains a board table and an A640 path, selected for "xiaomi,raphael"
(sweet_a630_probe); the a630 path keeps its values and behaviour.

Board values (SM8150; Linux sm8150.dtsi, gpucc-/gcc-sm8150.c; raphael's
reserved-memory): GPU 0x02c00000, GMU 0x02c6a000, gpucc 0x02c90000 (same
register offsets as SDM845), GPU SMMU (MMU-500) 0x02ca0000, PDC
0x0b290000/0x0b490000, cmd-db 0x85f20000, gcc_ddrss_gpu_axi 0x71154, chip
id 0x06040001, stream IDs GPU 0 mask 0x401 / GMU 5 mask 0x400, zap carve-out
pil_gpu_region 0x98f15000 (a640_zap.mdt + one relocatable PT_LOAD, b02),
GPU levels 257/345/427/499.2/585 MHz at RPMh 64/128/192/224/256.

The A640 GMU is non-legacy (Linux a6xx_gmu.c), so beyond the addresses:
- CX power-up in the Xiaomi vendor order: AOP QMP mailbox (0x0c300000,
  doorbell 0x17c00000+0xc) with "{class: gpu, res: acd, value: 0}", host
  ARC votes of mx/cx/gfx/xo through a free APPS DRV2 active TCS (boot-arg
  sweetgpuvote=0 skips them), GPLL0 + GCC/gpucc branches, and the CX GDSC
  through "{class: clock, res: gpu_noc_wa}" (falls back to clearing
  SW_COLLAPSE).
- MMU-500: sACR.CACHE_LOCK cleared, no qsmmuv2 micro-MMU/impl-defs, CB ACTLR
  next-page prefetch off; refuses a globally disabled SMMU (sCR0.CLIENTPD).
  When the CX GDSC was off (the SMMU unpowered), it is reset like
  arm_smmu_device_reset: on raphael its SMR/S2CR/context-bank registers held
  power-on junk after the CX power-up (first hardware run, 2026-11-06).
- HFI replies: the MSGQ interrupt bit or a non-empty message queue.
- MMU-500 has no SCTLR.ASIDPNE (read back 0 on raphael, second run): not set
  there; SMR/S2CR readback checks only CBNDX and TYPE on the A640.
- GMU memory: icache/dcache regions at GMU VA 0x4000-0x7ffff; block-format
  firmware loader (a640_gmu.bin: ITCM, icache, DTCM incl. the version words,
  dcache) with TCM readback; HFI v2 image check (DTCM 0xffc major 2).
- GMU registers: Linux fence range (0xa << 18) | 0xa0, interrupts cleared,
  chip id packed into HFI_SFR_ADDR; boot handshake as before (this image
  answers the legacy 0xbabeface).
- RPMh as Linux a6xx_gmu_rpmh_init for the a640 family: the PDC's third TCS
  command votes 0x30090 (xo.lvl on raphael's cmd-db, not gfx.lvl 0x30050),
  then a6xx_rpmh_stop before the RSC wake. After the start: CB0 faults, RSC
  state, the GMU log and a DTCM before/after comparison (did the CM3 run).
- HFI commands clear a stale message-queue interrupt before sending and keep
  waiting after a wake-up without their ACK (a stale bit lost H2F_MSG_START's
  ACK on one boot: GPU not kept up).
- GMU pages privileged-only (AP[2:1] 00, Linux IOMMU_PRIV): an EL0-writable
  page is implicitly PXN and the A640 GMU executes from its icache region.
  sweetgmuvar=N selects the older choices for experiments: 1 gfx.lvl, 2 no
  rpmh_stop, 4 vendor fence 0x80a008a0, 8 EL0 GMU pages, 16 context faults
  terminate.
- HFI v2: queue ids 0-3, packets padded to 4 dwords (0xfafafafa), reads
  aligned, ACK type 1, F2H error messages printed; FW_VER (2.0), PERF_TBL v2
  (all levels, ACD 0xffffffff), BW_VOTE_TBL with two levels built from the
  live cmd-db BCMs (SH0/MC0/ACV, SH2/SN15/SN3, VCD-sorted commit bits),
  FEATURE_CTRL (ECP off), CORE_FW_START; GX on = GX_BW_PERF_VOTE, OOB GPU_SET
  (bits 30/31), H2F_MSG_START, keep-alive, GX/fence polls; level changes by
  GX_BW_PERF_VOTE; slumber by PREPARE_SLUMBER; no host SPTPRAC.
- CP hw_init: GBIF halt release, secure TSB range cleared, GBIF QSB/QoS
  instead of VBIF, ROQ 0x02000140, prim FIFO 0x400 << 11, hang detect
  0xcfffff; no A640 clock-gating table yet (sweetgpuhwcg is ignored).
- GPU_ID/CHIP_ID parameters and the IOKit properties report 640/0x06040001.

Sources: register numbers, values and order only (no code copied), from the
Xiaomi nabu (SM8150, same a640_gmu.bin) vendor KGSL sequence recorded in
zzweiqing/UniXNU-nabu gpu/a640, Linux v6.12 a6xx_gmu.c, a6xx_hfi.c,
a6xx_gpu.c, a6xx_catalog.c, gpucc-sm8150.c, gcc-sm8150.c, sm8150.dtsi.
Firmware goes into the ADT: tools/adt-gpufw.py --gpu a640.

